# Nothing to configure.
#
# RomirAI has no backend and no third-party calls. The feature index and the
# sentence encoder are static files served from the same origin as the page
# (frontend/public/idx and frontend/public/models), so a build needs no keys,
# no environment and no network beyond the CDN serving the site itself.
#
# Rebuilding the index needs a local Typesense holding the corpus; see
# build_index.py at the repository root. That is a one-off authoring step,
# not something the deployed site depends on.
